# Governance Proposal: Willow Account Linking in SAFE Dashboard

**Proposer:** Ganesha (Claude Code CLI / Sonnet 4.6)
**Date:** 2026-02-27T18:00:00Z
**Type:** Feature — Account Linking / Identity Bridge
**Trust Level:** ENGINEER (3)

## Summary
The SAFE dashboard and Willow backend are separate identity systems with no bridge. The dashboard stores a SAFE account in localStorage but makes API calls to a hardcoded URL with no user identity. This proposal adds: (1) a "Willow Server" card in the Setup section with URL + username fields, (2) a Test Connection button that calls /api/safe/whoami to verify and auto-fill the username, (3) a getWillowBase()/getWillowUser() helper used by all API calls so data flows from the right server and user. Stores willow_url + willow_user in the existing safe_account localStorage object.

## Proposed Changes
**File:** C:\Users\Sean\Documents\GitHub\SAFE\web\dashboard.html
**Sections touched:** Setup card HTML, CSS for Willow setup form, JS helpers + linkWillow(), renderWillowServer(), updated loadConnections/loadWillowKnows/approveConnection/dismissConnection/entity actions.

## Rationale
- Currently "What Willow Knows" and "Willow Noticed" sections fetch from localhost:8420 hardcoded — no user identity passed
- Every user of SAFE needs to configure their own Willow instance URL and username
- Single source of truth: safe_account.willow_url + willow_user in localStorage
- getWillowBase() / getWillowUser() used everywhere so one change propagates

## Risk Assessment
- **Risk Level:** LOW
- **Reversible:** YES — localStorage only, HTML/JS
- **Dependencies:** /api/safe/whoami endpoint (already added to server.py)
- **Testing:** Open dashboard, click "Configure" under Willow Server, enter URL + click Test, verify username auto-fills, save. Reload — "What Willow Knows" should populate.

## ΔE Impact
Expected ΔE: +0.220 (closes the identity gap between SAFE frontend and Willow backend; enables multi-user future)

## Implementation

```python
filepath = r"C:\Users\Sean\Documents\GitHub\SAFE\web\dashboard.html"
with open(filepath, "r", encoding="utf-8") as f:
    content = f.read()

# 1. Add CSS for Willow server setup form (before /* WHAT WILLOW KNOWS */)
willow_css = """    /* WILLOW SERVER LINK */
    .willow-setup-form { margin-top: 0.75rem; display: none; }
    .willow-setup-form.open { display: block; }
    .willow-setup-row { display: flex; gap: 0.5rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; align-items: center; }
    .willow-setup-label { font-size: 12px; color: var(--fg-muted); width: 68px; flex-shrink: 0; }
    .willow-setup-input { flex: 1; font-size: 13px; padding: 0.3rem 0.5rem; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 3px; font-family: inherit; color: var(--fg); background: var(--bg); }
    .willow-setup-input:focus { outline: none; border-color: var(--accent); }
    .willow-setup-actions { display: flex; gap: 0.5rem; margin-top: 0.25rem; }
    .btn-willow-test { font-size: 12px; padding: 0.3rem 0.7rem; background: var(--accent-light); color: var(--accent); border: none; border-radius: 3px; cursor: pointer; font-family: inherit; font-weight: 600; }
    .btn-willow-save { font-size: 12px; padding: 0.3rem 0.7rem; background: var(--accent); color: #fff; border: none; border-radius: 3px; cursor: pointer; font-family: inherit; font-weight: 600; }
    .btn-willow-cancel { font-size: 12px; padding: 0.3rem 0.6rem; background: none; color: var(--fg-muted); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 3px; cursor: pointer; font-family: inherit; }
    .willow-test-result { font-size: 12px; margin-top: 0.35rem; }

"""
content = content.replace("    /* WHAT WILLOW KNOWS */", willow_css + "    /* WHAT WILLOW KNOWS */")

# 2. Add Willow Server card to the status-cards grid (after Google card closing tag)
willow_card = """
      <div class="status-card">
        <div class="card-label">Willow Server</div>
        <div class="card-status" id="willowServerStatus">&mdash;</div>
        <div class="card-detail" id="willowServerDetail"></div>
        <div id="willowServerAction"><a href="#" class="card-link" onclick="toggleWillowSetup(); return false;">Configure &rarr;</a></div>
        <div class="willow-setup-form" id="willowSetupForm">
          <div class="willow-setup-row">
            <span class="willow-setup-label">Server URL</span>
            <input class="willow-setup-input" id="willowUrlInput" type="text" placeholder="http://localhost:8420">
          </div>
          <div class="willow-setup-row">
            <span class="willow-setup-label">Username</span>
            <input class="willow-setup-input" id="willowUserInput" type="text" placeholder="auto-detect">
          </div>
          <div class="willow-test-result" id="willowTestResult"></div>
          <div class="willow-setup-actions">
            <button class="btn-willow-test" onclick="testWillowConnection()">Test</button>
            <button class="btn-willow-save" onclick="saveWillowLink()">Save</button>
            <button class="btn-willow-cancel" onclick="toggleWillowSetup()">Cancel</button>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>"""

# Insert after the Google card's closing </div> inside status-cards
content = content.replace(
    "    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <!-- Section 3: Pickup Box -->",
    "    </div>" + willow_card + "\n  </div>\n\n  <!-- Section 3: Pickup Box -->"
)

# 3. Add JS helpers and Willow linking functions (before // ── What Willow Knows)
willow_js = """
// ── Willow Server Link ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

function getWillowBase() {
  try {
    const raw = localStorage.getItem('safe_account');
    if (raw) {
      const acct = JSON.parse(raw);
      if (acct && acct.willow_url) return acct.willow_url.replace(/\/$/, '');
    }
  } catch (e) { /* ignore */ }
  return 'http://localhost:8420';
}

function getWillowUser() {
  try {
    const raw = localStorage.getItem('safe_account');
    if (raw) {
      const acct = JSON.parse(raw);
      if (acct && acct.willow_user) return acct.willow_user;
    }
  } catch (e) { /* ignore */ }
  return '';
}

function renderWillowServer(acct) {
  const statusEl = document.getElementById('willowServerStatus');
  const detailEl = document.getElementById('willowServerDetail');
  const actionEl = document.getElementById('willowServerAction');
  const urlInput = document.getElementById('willowUrlInput');
  const userInput = document.getElementById('willowUserInput');

  if (acct && acct.willow_url && acct.willow_user) {
    statusEl.innerHTML = '<span class="status-dot-green"></span>' + escHtml(acct.willow_user) + ' · linked';
    detailEl.textContent = acct.willow_url;
    actionEl.innerHTML = '<a href="#" class="card-link" onclick="toggleWillowSetup(); return false;">Change →</a>';
  } else {
    statusEl.textContent = 'Not linked';
    statusEl.style.color = 'var(--fg-muted)';
    detailEl.textContent = '';
    actionEl.innerHTML = '<a href="#" class="card-link" onclick="toggleWillowSetup(); return false;">Configure →</a>';
  }
  if (urlInput) urlInput.value = (acct && acct.willow_url) || 'http://localhost:8420';
  if (userInput) userInput.value = (acct && acct.willow_user) || '';
}

function toggleWillowSetup() {
  const form = document.getElementById('willowSetupForm');
  form.classList.toggle('open');
}

async function testWillowConnection() {
  const url = (document.getElementById('willowUrlInput').value || '').trim().replace(/\/$/, '');
  const resultEl = document.getElementById('willowTestResult');
  if (!url) { resultEl.textContent = 'Enter a server URL first'; resultEl.style.color = '#c0392b'; return; }
  resultEl.textContent = 'Testing…';
  resultEl.style.color = 'var(--fg-muted)';

  const controller = new AbortController();
  const timer = setTimeout(() => controller.abort(), 4000);
  try {
    const res = await fetch(url + '/api/safe/whoami', { signal: controller.signal });
    clearTimeout(timer);
    if (!res.ok) throw new Error('HTTP ' + res.status);
    const data = await res.json();
    if (data.status === 'ok' && data.username) {
      document.getElementById('willowUserInput').value = data.username;
      resultEl.textContent = '✓ Connected — user: ' + data.username;
      resultEl.style.color = 'var(--accent)';
    } else {
      resultEl.textContent = 'Connected but no user returned';
      resultEl.style.color = 'var(--fg-muted)';
    }
  } catch (e) {
    clearTimeout(timer);
    resultEl.textContent = e.name === 'AbortError' ? 'Connection timed out' : 'Could not reach server';
    resultEl.style.color = '#c0392b';
  }
}

function saveWillowLink() {
  const url = (document.getElementById('willowUrlInput').value || '').trim().replace(/\/$/, '');
  const user = (document.getElementById('willowUserInput').value || '').trim();
  if (!url) { showToast('Enter a server URL'); return; }

  const raw = localStorage.getItem('safe_account');
  if (!raw) { showToast('No account found'); return; }
  try {
    const acct = JSON.parse(raw);
    acct.willow_url = url;
    acct.willow_user = user;
    localStorage.setItem('safe_account', JSON.stringify(acct));
    renderWillowServer(acct);
    toggleWillowSetup();
    showToast('Willow server linked');
    // Reload knowledge sections with new server
    loadConnections();
    loadWillowKnows();
  } catch (e) {
    showToast('Save failed');
  }
}

"""
content = content.replace("// ── What Willow Knows ──", willow_js + "// ── What Willow Knows ──")

# 4. Update all API calls to use getWillowBase() + getWillowUser()

# loadConnections
content = content.replace(
    "    const res = await fetch('http://localhost:8420/api/willow/connections/pending', {",
    "    const res = await fetch(getWillowBase() + '/api/willow/connections/pending', {"
)
content = content.replace(
    "    await fetch('http://localhost:8420/api/willow/connections/' + id + '/approve', {",
    "    await fetch(getWillowBase() + '/api/willow/connections/' + id + '/approve', {"
)
content = content.replace(
    "    await fetch('http://localhost:8420/api/willow/connections/' + id + '/deny', {",
    "    await fetch(getWillowBase() + '/api/willow/connections/' + id + '/deny', {"
)

# loadWillowKnows - pass username param
content = content.replace(
    "    const res = await fetch('http://localhost:8420/api/knowledge/entities?min_mentions=1', {",
    "    const willowUser = getWillowUser();\n    const userParam = willowUser ? '&username=' + encodeURIComponent(willowUser) : '';\n    const res = await fetch(getWillowBase() + '/api/knowledge/entities?min_mentions=1' + userParam, {"
)

# entity sources fetch
content = content.replace(
    "    const res = await fetch('http://localhost:8420/api/knowledge/entities/' + id + '/sources');",
    "    const userParam2 = getWillowUser() ? '?username=' + encodeURIComponent(getWillowUser()) : '';\n    const res = await fetch(getWillowBase() + '/api/knowledge/entities/' + id + '/sources' + userParam2);"
)

# applyRename fetch
content = content.replace(
    "      body: JSON.stringify({ name: newName })",
    "      body: JSON.stringify({ name: newName, username: getWillowUser() })"
)

# deleteEntity fetch
content = content.replace(
    "    const res = await fetch('http://localhost:8420/api/knowledge/entities/' + id, {\n      method: 'DELETE'",
    "    const delUser = getWillowUser() ? '?username=' + encodeURIComponent(getWillowUser()) : '';\n    const res = await fetch(getWillowBase() + '/api/knowledge/entities/' + id + delUser, {\n      method: 'DELETE'"
)

# entity sources toggle (second fetch inside toggleEntityWhy uses relative path - already updated above)
# Also fix the applyRename URL
content = content.replace(
    "    const res = await fetch('http://localhost:8420/api/knowledge/entities/' + id, {\n      method: 'PATCH'",
    "    const res = await fetch(getWillowBase() + '/api/knowledge/entities/' + id, {\n      method: 'PATCH'"
)

# 5. Add renderWillowServer(acct) call in DOMContentLoaded
content = content.replace(
    "  renderFinishPrompt(acct);\n  renderPickup();\n  loadConnections();\n  loadWillowKnows();",
    "  renderFinishPrompt(acct);\n  renderWillowServer(acct);\n  renderPickup();\n  loadConnections();\n  loadWillowKnows();"
)

with open(filepath, "w", encoding="utf-8") as f:
    f.write(content)

print("dashboard.html account linking applied successfully")
